pos/aurakimjh/archscope/zipball/v0.4.0-rc.2","body":"**RC2 artifacts refreshed on 2026-11-20 (Asia/Seoul).** The version and download URL are unchanged; the packaged source is `fe92b5bcfd1fdcd3595b30a9d25d2204a8c31937`. Re-download the files if using the original RC2 build. The detailed refresh notes below were prepared on 2026-11-19.\n\n# ArchScope v0.4.0-rc.2\n\nThis is a **prerelease for controlled evaluation**, preparing the 0.4.0 feature\nline. It includes RC1 diagnostics and Windows HTTP work, the compact desktop\nribbon and five UI languages, plus subsequent fixes and verification tooling. It is not a declaration of complete reference-tool parity or\nuniversal production acceptance.\n\n## RC2 refresh — 2026-11-19\n\nThis existing prerelease is being refreshed at the user's request, retaining\nthe RC2 version and download address. Download the refreshed files again;\nthe application source/build identity changes even though the version stays\n0.4.0-rc.2. The original 2026-11-17 source was\n`9dc0c2390a7602125af5f53401ad3b3f70112824`; its publication evidence is preserved.\n\n- Arthas/async-profiler HTML now decodes absolute frame records and compressed\n  constant-pool/delta records, preserving sample weights without executing\n  imported JavaScript.\n- A single text file containing repeated `jstack` or `jcmd Thread.print`\n  captures automatically expands to multi-dump analysis and the multi-dump UI.\n- GC pause and heap tooltips show event timestamps/uptime, GC type and measured\n  pause duration for remark/cleanup/full phases. Heap timing works with the\n  pause overlay off and without an occupancy measurement; unknown duration is\n  not zero. Unified completed pause summaries without heap fields are parsed.\n\nOwned JDK21 repeated-capture inputs and four scoped macOS JVM-input checks pass.\nGC chart builders using Go analysis output pass nine real-browser mouse-hover\nchecks. Native macOS GC hover remains unverified because the diagnostic WebView\nwas hidden and did not paint; original user inputs and Windows runtime coverage\nremain separate. The acceptance limits below are unchanged.\n\n## Downloads and versions\n\n| Artifact | Target |\n| --- | --- |\n| macOS DMG / app ZIP | Apple Silicon arm64, macOS 12+ |\n| Windows installer / executable ZIP | Windows x64; WebView2 required |\n| Linux DEB / RPM / raw binary archive | x64; GTK4 and WebKitGTK 6 runtime |\n| archscope-docs.zip | English/Korean manuals, reference documents and repository examples |\n| archscope-conformance-v1.zip | Synthetic offline conformance corpus |\n| SHA256SUMS | Checksums for the attached release files |\n\nApplication/About version: **0.4.0-rc.2**. Windows numeric file version:\n**0.4.0.2**. macOS bundle short version: **0.4.0**, build **4002**.\nLinux package metadata uses the RC version. Windows x86 testing does not imply\nan x86 installer is included in this release.\n\nThe workflow can use ad-hoc macOS signing when Developer ID/notarization\ncredentials are absent; notarization is conditional on configured credentials.\nWindows artifacts are not Authenticode-signed by this workflow. Required\nplatform runtimes must already be available for offline use; the standard\nWindows installer may bootstrap WebView2 if missing.\n\n## Changes since RC1\n\n- Compact ribbon with responsive groups, visible icons and saved expanded,\n  tab-only and hidden states; shared native/HTTP command routing.\n- English, Korean, Japanese, Simplified Chinese and Traditional Chinese UI.\n  Windows Settings shortcut routing and selected contrast defects are fixed.\n- Windows x64/x86 seven-unit native chart Saves and distinct-file import\n  screening, with original raw failures preserved alongside passing cases.\n- Completed-file publication and bounded partial-JSON/Windows sharing-violation\n  polling for layout-audit receipts; deterministic batching and UTF-8 source regression checks.\n- Aggregate-only owned renderer memory tooling and new Mac/Docker attribution\n  results. The new collector has not yet executed on native Windows.\n\n## Included work\n\n- File-based CPU/wall/lock profiles, original py-spy/Speedscope/pprof evidence,\n  canonical drilldown, source references and case-backed baseline comparison.\n- Access, GC, JFR/native-memory, exceptions, multi-runtime thread dumps,\n  Jennifer MSA, traces, Chrome/V8 CPU and Lighthouse analysis.\n- Workspace cases, search, metric history, system/perf/limited BPF, runtime,\n  database/socket, benchmark/crash, LLM/serving and CPU/GPU evidence workflows.\n  Producer/version support is limited to the documented qualified inputs.\n- Windows explicit-proxy HTTP/1.x capture, HAR and supported session formats,\n  bounded retention, process attribution, inspectors, annotations, session\n  comparison/correlation and an explicit-send Request Builder.\n- Request/response body capture only where actual SEC-10 preflight permits it,\n  with default-off opt-in, redaction, preview bounds and explicit missing,\n  unsupported, encoded or truncated states.\n- Input/result invalidation, x86 profile weight fixes, physical-unit chart/CSV\n  exports, stable bounded PowerPoint summaries, accessibility fixes and the\n  detailed screen-by-screen user manual.\n- Repeated-import retention fixes and finite memory qualification. Historical\n  growth failures remain preserved; later passing windows do not prove that\n  every workload is leak-free.\n\n## Remaining qualification\n\nThe tracker retains **T-601 REVIEW, T-611 REVIEW, T-613 PENDING, T-627 REVIEW,\nT-663 REVIEW, T-664 REVIEW, T-654 TODO and T-662 TODO**. This RC does not close them.\n\n- Transparent/WinDivert, proxy-ignoring clients, services and cross-session\n  capture reach still need matching isolated native qualification.\n- Vendor/foreign early-bound COM, session cookies and clean-host registration\n  lifecycle remain separate from the tested automation contracts.\n- Full original V7.6.4 exchange/display/export parity, actual IME composition,\n  drag interactions, remaining format/body conditions, actual OS DPI/locale\n  and the full result/provider/keyboard/reference matrix are incomplete.\n  WebView zoom is not OS DPI coverage.\n- Body-enabled Windows x64 remains subject to its actual preflight result.\n  No dump, trust or security-policy bypass is provided.\n- Ordinary unique-file imports pass the received Windows x64/x86 finite memory\n  screens. **Body-rich imports still fail**: tree slopes 4.801 MiB/cycle (x64)\n  and 8.764 MiB/cycle (x86) exceed the original 4 MiB/cycle limit. Renderer-private\n  growth requires actual Windows allocation diagnosis and ordinary-build\n  revalidation after a cause-specific change. Bounded workspace ownership and\n  explicit-GC diagnostics do not establish an allocation cause or a passing\n  ordinary renderer. The original budget is unchanged.\n- The changed receipt publisher/runner and new aggregate collector need native\n  Windows execution; compile/controlled-I/O tests are separate. Longer memory\n  runs, real Windows disk exhaustion, power-loss recovery, clean-host install\n  and actual RC1-to-RC2 upgrade/migration remain beyond their scoped receipts.\n- Actual two-GPU CUDA/NCCL distributed inference and natural nonzero-swap /\n  elevated-pressure input remain unavailable. CPU/structural fixtures and\n  observed zero swap do not establish those cases.\n- The original independent CONDITIONAL review dispositions are preserved;\n  local remediation is not a new independent PASS.\n\n## Compatibility and validation\n\nExisting AnalysisResult/data contract meanings remain intact. Application\nprerelease comparison uses SemVer; numeric data/adapter/extension versions keep\ntheir strict existing contract. The unchanged signed bootstrap pack permits\napplication versions before stable 0.4.0, so this RC remains eligible. A final\n0.4.0 release needs a newly qualified compatible signed pack; the range is not\nsilently widened.\n\nRelease preparation runs full local Go tests/race/vet, frontend state/build,\nresource/version checks and packaging checks. Hosted Engine Native, Windows\nGUI smoke and all three packaging targets are checked before tag publication;\npackaging/launch smoke does not establish clean-host installation or upgrade.\nThese checks do not substitute for the remaining native acceptance matrix.\n\nRead the [Korean release notes](https://github.com/aurakimjh/archscope/blob/v0.4.0-rc.2/docs/ko/releases/v0.4.0-rc.2.md),\n[English manual](https://github.com/aurakimjh/archscope/blob/v0.4.0-rc.2/docs/en/USER_GUIDE.md),\n[Korean manual](https://github.com/aurakimjh/archscope/blob/v0.4.0-rc.2/docs/ko/USER_GUIDE.md)\nand [work tracker](https://github.com/aurakimjh/archscope/blob/v0.4.0-rc.2/work_status.md)\nfor exact scope and source evidence.\n"}